s highlight band off at the list's edges and the lit name's first letter with it - on the narrow sheet the band's fixed margin also ran 2px into the border, and its left padding stood the lit name 2px left of the rest. So it measures the lit row too (band edge to edge, name whole and unmoved) and the cap still clipping a six-row pile downward at a 360px window. 18 checks, 3 shots. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/chatChanProbe.mjs` mounts the REAL chat panel over the real sheet in Chromium, on the desktop skin and the touch skin, at the sheet's 440px box and the narrowest a phone gives (352px), and reads back what a fake cannot: World, Region, Party, Local and the Social button in ONE bar inside the box with no tab's name cut; every tab's hover; the field's placeholder following the tab and the Region tab's by the region's name; an aside in `(( ))` drawn leaning and dimmed beside a line in character; the peek's Party mark in the party's green and a notice with none; a roll in its own colour and the dice's words beside a typed line that only reads like one (DICE1); `/help`'s 'read' answer clearing the field with the chat left open; and EMOTE1's - the form row at every width with the field never under the narrowest the chat had before the emoji button (the touch skin's 115px at a 320px phone), the picker's round trip, the edge where the button gives way (the smallest box a drag makes keeps it, a pixel under does not), an action's face, and a joined family drawn as ONE glyph after the wire's sanitizer. IT FOUND TWO DEFECTS: four tabs and the Social button asked 373px of a 350px bar, pushing Social past the box's edge; and with three tabs unread they asked 468px of the sheet's own 440 - where the first fix (tabs shrinking to an ellipsis) MEASURED as fitting and a screenshot showed "PARTY..." beside a clipped smear of badge. Its judges now read what the eye does: a label whole inside its button (the text's own box, not scrollWidth, which clip does not move), every unread dot whole, Social always in the box. The tabs stand in a strip of their own that never squeezes a tab (a phone's scrolls sideways), an unread count is a dot with the number as the tab's spoken name, and a box under 400px (a container query - CHAT-SIZE lets the box be narrow on a wide screen) closes the labels up. At 440, 352 and a 320px phone's 292, on both skins, bare and with three tabs unread - 75 checks. EMOTE1's own run found two more: the button took a touch field to 67px at 320 (the touch skin has no button now - a phone keyboard has an emoji key) and a desktop one to 93px in a box the screen forced below the drag's minimum; and the first cut of the rule that yields it there asked the drag's width of a container query, which measures inside the box's border, and hid the button at the smallest box a drag makes. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/chatSizeProbe.mjs` drags the REAL grip with the real mouse over the chat's and the friends panel's real sheets in Chromium, at 1440x900 and 900x900, and reads the layout back - the box's width, the list's height, a line's and a roster row's computed size, Send's (a thumb's, unscaled), the grip against the Close button, the friends panel's rectangle against the box's (beside at 1440, under at 900, over it at neither), after a reload, and after a double click. IT FOUND TWO DEFECTS ON ITS FIRST RUN that the fake could not: the grip stood at the end of the form's row, which is the conversation column's corner and not the box's (the roster stands beyond it), and the list grew 132px for a 120px drag (its clientHeight carries its own padding, which the height the sheet sets does not). 24 checks. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/chatScrollProbe.mjs` drives the REAL chat panel over the real sheet in Chromium and reads the list's own scrollTop against its range after each thing a player does - the first open, an open after lines came in while closed, an open after reading history and closing, a line under a reader at the bottom, three under a reader who scrolled up (not yanked, the bar says 3), the bar's click - plain and with every line wearing a badge that wraps it. It exists because Starempire42's report is about a real scroll box, which node cannot lay out; Chromium keeps a hidden scroller's offset, so the engines that drop it are test/chatscroll.test.js's half. 12 checks. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/chatFitProbe.mjs` stands the REAL chat panel (createChatPanel over a real ChatLog, CHAT_CSS over the enhanced sheet) in Chromium at a desktop and a phone-landscape viewport with twenty-four long names wearing titles and glyphs, and MEASURES: the box is 299 px with three names and 299 px with twenty-four, the column exactly as tall as the conversation, 437 px of list in 235, every row one line (16-17 px against a 16.2 px line), eight names cut with an ellipsis, and the chat lines wearing their authors' badges. It exists because Mac's report was a screenshot and every one of its three sentences is about pixels: a pin can say a rule reads `nowrap` and a column is `absolute`, and only a layout engine can say the box stopped growing. 12 checks, 2 shots. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/noticeFitProbe.mjs` draws the enhanced NOTICE PANELS through `drawEnhancedNotice` - the entry every box and every toast goes through - over the real ENHANCED_CSS in Chromium, at desktop, narrow and phone widths, and MEASURES each one's border-box width: a one-line notice, the status readout, a long quest box and a toast come back 210 / 450 / 520 / 339 px at 1280 wide, four widths where NOTICE-FIT found one. It exists because kurkku asked for "the sizing of the boxes to properly adjust for the text" and width is a thing about pixels - a pin can say the rule reads `max-width` and still not say that "You are healthy." hugs its line while a four-paragraph box still wraps at the cap. IT LIED ON ITS FIRST RUN and the picture is how it was caught: the panels photographed 46px off the right edge with a live transform, because NOTICE_WATCHDOG_MS had correctly swept a panel nobody was drawing - a harness that does not do what the host does measures its own artefact, so it PUMPS the draw on rAF the way a host does. 12 measurements, 3 shots. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `npm run blood` (tools/bloodProbe.mjs) drives `createHitEffects` and `drawBillboards` over a texture whose colour is known, in a real WebGL2 context, and reads the pixel back at five lighting states. MAC-BUG W6: and then installs the Enhanced Lighting lane and reads a sprite and a mark side by side at four more - the rows where the mark came back at 25 against 69 and 2 against 17 while every classic row was green. 26 checks (AUDIT BLOOD3 F10: and the MENISCUS is drawn now - the same mark against a uniform-thickness one under a grazing sun, the difference banded by radius, which is the one law this arc took to main with no picture; the film's own rows, banded by RADIUS inside the mark's silhouette rather than by brightness, which was sorting the alpha-faded rim into the thin bucket and measuring the blend). It exists because MAC-BUG W4 ("Also blood is black") could not be settled by reading: it clears the pool, the texture KEY (`380_0#0` is minted in scenes/dataPipeline.js and asked for in render/renderer.js, and nothing had ever checked the two agree), the shader's emission arm, and anything specific to blood - a plain sprite in the same dungeon light comes back the same 20,2,2. 9 checks. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/setUiProbe.mjs` draws the REAL pack (`createInventoryWindow`, the enhanced skin) and the REAL HUD with a kit worn through the game's own equip - six of Dagon's Brand and its sword, two of Ruhn's Regalia, a Mora helm and a Nocturnal cuirass carried - online at Renown 12, at a desktop, a laptop and a phone: the doll's strip (two lines, "7/9" and "2/9", their