the pseudo-locale, and no page errors. 36 checks. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/classicTextProbe.mjs` (L10N2) draws a line of French, German, Polish, Vietnamese, Russian, Greek, Japanese, Simplified and Traditional Chinese and Korean through `ui/text.js` drawText on a REAL WebGL renderer, over a stand-in FONT0003 with blank glyphs and no ARENA2, and reads the pixels back: each language a face over its script's fonts (Han by region), every character a glyph grown on demand, ink where the line is and ending where its measured advance does, a full-width character one GlyphHeight wide, and English - left to Daggerfall's own glyphs - drawing no face. 45 checks, one picture (`PROBE_SHOTS`). PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser and a DFU translation pack on disk, which is never committed): `PACK_DIR=... node tools/translationPackProbe.mjs` (L10N3b) installs the pack through Settings > Interface's Translation pack row in Chromium - its folder, then its .zip - and reads the game's tables back: its Internal_Strings and TEXT.RSC rows live, the language told its pack, its FONT0003 the face drawn, all of it still there after a reload, and gone after Remove. 13 checks with the French pack (354 files; 352 from its zip). PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/lootBannerProbe.mjs` draws the REAL loot banners (`drawLootBanners` handed a player entity, as drawHud hands it) over the real enhanced HUD and a real notice toast in Chromium at 1440x900, 1024x700 and a 390x844 phone, the pieces minted by the game's own producers (a Rare, an Exalted Legendary, a Legendary card; an Aetheric, an Artifact and the Hourlock; a burst of six), and reads: every banner at the right edge and on the screen, none over the notices, none scrolling sideways, every name in its tier's colour, the top tiers big and taller than the rest, the best of a burst standing first, never more than three. 183 checks, 9 shots. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/cardPanelsProbe.mjs` (CARDS-PLUS, `11-Multiplayer/Tavern-Cards.md` section 38) mounts the REAL Hold'em and Iliac Hand panels over the card lab's table through their own painters and models - Iliac Hand's setup (a friendly game), a turn with a card staged and one picked, its end; Hold'em's buy-in at a gold table, a hand at the flop with four chairs, a full table's river and its showdown - on Enhanced Plus, the classic skin and the DFO Grimoire dress, at 1280x760, a 1000x560 window, 390x844 and 360x740 phones and an 844x390 phone under a finger (AUDIT CARDS-PLUS C5), with the launcher's own Pixelify Sans laid (the probe's browser has no route to the game's font request), and reads: the panel's words, title and presses in the game's face (the dress's under the dress) and no face of the panel's own - no serif, and under the dress exactly the dress's own stack (AUDIT CARDS-PLUS C5: the base skipped the dress, whose stack ends in Georgia); the kit's carved frame; the panel on the screen and nothing wider than it, no lane past its holding; no lane, little card or note wearing the enhanced sheet's bare `.row`, `.card` or `.note`; the hand painted at its 80px tile face; the log at its newest standing on a whole line; the fold on the screen to press, putting the table's words away and back with the line and the presses still drawn; and (AUDIT CARDS-PLUS C5, which found 100 of its first 314 checks running over nothing) every part a check reads counted there, the pot inside its board, each state either panel marks drawn apart from its rest in every look, no card over another. IT FOUND TWO DEFECTS BEFORE IT WAS WRITTEN DOWN, as the scratch harness it grew from: the log's top line half cut when scrolled (a scrolling padding, and a line holding a 5 grown a pixel by the five's own face - the lines are fixed boxes now, the gap their first's margin), and a regular's tile and a seat's name cut to an ellipsis (they wrap). 1,690 checks, 105 shots.
